    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0397" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v06p1/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">RA files, lot 58 D 374, “CSC Loan
                    Negotiations”</note>
                <head>No. 191<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Foreign Operations
                        Administration (Stassen) to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-01-05">January 5, 1954</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Foster</hi>: You will recall the background of
                    the President’s conference with Jean Monnet of the European Coal and Steel
                    Community on June 3, 1953, and his subsequent letter of June 15.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d191-f1"/></p>
                <p>The follow-up conferences with Mr. Monnet in Paris during the NATO
                        meetings<anchor n="2" xml:id="d191-f2"/> lead me to make the recommendation
                    reflected in the attached memorandum.</p>
                <p>I would appreciate your preliminary comments prior to firming up the proposal for
                    the President’s action.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harold E. Stassen</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d191-a1.xml" xpointer="d191-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d191-a2.xml" xpointer="d191-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d191-f1" n="1" xml:id="d191-f1-content">
                <p>For information concerning Monnet’s visit to Washington June 3–4, and the
                    exchange of correspondence between President Eisenhower and Senator Wiley and
                    Representative Chiperfield concerning Monnet’s visit, see <ref target="#d169"
                        >Documents 169</ref> and <ref target="#d172">172</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d191-f2" n="2" xml:id="d191-f2-content">
                <p>Concerning these conversations in Paris, Dec. 13–15, see <ref target="#d187"
                        >Document 187</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
